69 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (since such attacks do not typically bring down the service, but instead lead the receiver to accept incorrect yet believable navigation information. Thus, the attacked entity may function properly relying on invalid positional or temporal information and therefore, such kinds of attacks are specifically challenging to discover. Spoofing detection via Signal Processing: The diagnostic techniques for detecting GNSS spoofing have remained largely unchanged over the years and have included a blended use of signal processing \(e.g., signal power, angle-of-arrival, cryptographic authentication, and multi-sensor consistency checks\). Although successful in some cases, they typically involve costly hardware, multiple antennas, or knowledge of attack profile. What is more, their accuracy may weaken in complex environments with multipath propagation, dynamic motion, or advanced attacks that closely replicate the behaviors of legitimate signals [5]. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
70 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (The rapid development of artificial intelligence and machine learning capabilities hold new potential to develop GNSS spoofing mitigation approaches that are able to adapt and learn from patterns and experiences [6]. In general, data-driven models can learn intricate and nonlinear relationships between signal features that may not be easily captured by rule-based methods. Machine learning models accomplish this by learning earlier signal patterns and identifying the minutest of variations to statistical characteristics caused by spoofing even when counterfeit signals have almost similar characteristics to authentic signals. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
71 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 49 0 R
/E (In light, this paper aims to explore the use of complex machine learning models \(DNN, RF and XGBoost\) in GNSS spoof detection from a practical standpoint, using real world data. Special attention is paid to reducing false-negative mistakes taking into consideration their negative and immediate impact on navigation safety. Based on systematic comparative analysis and real-time [7],[8], [9]. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
