/E (The research employs real-time GNSS signal datasets that are comprised of real as well as spoofed GNSS signal's due to it being very important that only real GNSS signal datasets, as in, the signal datasets from real-life environments are utilized because they reflect the actual conditions under which the GNSS signals propagate, namely, thermal noise, multipath reflection of GNSS signals, atmospheric disturbances to the GNSS signals and inaccuracies related to GNSS hardware/receivers, all of which cannot be accurately represented with synthetic GNSS signal datasets. These GNSS Signal Datasets were collected from several publicly available data repositories that focus on )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
