/Title (Global Navigation Satellite Systems \(GNSS\) have become critical to the functioning of our modern technology-based societies through Positioning, Navigation and Timing \(PNT\). These services drive civilian and military applications ranging from smartphones navigation and fleet management to aviation essential systems, maritime navigation, as well as controlling autonomous unmanned platforms. Because critical and safety-relevant applications are increasingly based on GNSS there is a growing need to achieve integrity and reliability of satellite-based navigation. Finally, GNSS signals, while being a great technology to have offer very low-powered signals once they reach ground level and are susceptible. Spoofing attacks are especially harmful,)
